{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions","id":1166277,"title":"Some C20 Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-09T07:33:17-08:00","id":1166277,"title":"Some C20 Questions","content":"I'm planning on running a Changeling The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition campaign in the near future. I was a fan of the CWoD for years as a teenager, but haven't really picked it up much for over a decade. <br /> <br /> I was hoping that with the X20 editions a lot of the flaws from poor game design and unclear rules/systems would be fixed seeing as NWoD/CoD is fairly tight mechanically. Unfortunately that doesn't seem to be the case and now I have a ton of systems that need to be clarified and seemingly incomplete mechanics that I need explained.<br /> <br /> Some of the issues are C20 specific, while others may be more CWoD 20 general, but I'm just going to list them all and see what you guys can do to help out.<br /> <br /> Delaying/With holding actions - I think I understand this one. As I interpret it, when declaring actions in reverse initiative, if I choose to withhold my action, I am basically sacrificing my action that round in order to go first next round. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> Shields vs. firearms - I also think I get this one. So if I try to use my shield vs a gunshot, it says that I have to make a successful parry, but I don't subtract successes from the attacker's roll. So I assume this means that if someone shooting me got 4 successes on their attack roll, I would need to match those 4 successes on my parry roll to be able to use my shield soak. Correct?<br /> <br /> Mounted combat - C20 states that your Dex+Ride is the maximum pool you can use for combat actions when mounted, and that when my mount may lose control I have to make a reflexive ride roll. The problem with this is twofold. First Ride isn't a skill in C20 so I can't roll it, and second it doesn't say what attribute to roll for the roll to maintain control. I assume you can sub in Animal Ken for Ride, but what attribute would I roll to maintain control? It seems implied that this would also be Dex, but that makes no sense at all, as Strength or Charisma would likely be better options with what little I know about riding animals.<br /> <br /> Medicine ability - It doesn't actually do anything. There are no mechanics for how it can be used to treat injuries or diseases, so why even have it as an ability?<br /> <br /> Rhapsody - How much Glamour does it actually generate? Is it just the amount initially invested in the process, or is it one per success on the artist's creation roll? Either way it really doesn't seem worth doing, even before considering the non-mechanical in-game consequences of doing it. To even consider Rhapsody one would have to be both Evil (TM) and really dumb. So how can Rhapsody be made to be something actually tempting to try?<br /> <br /> Effects of Banality - p. 270 of C20 states several mechanical effects of Banality, but it is pretty unclear as to under what circumstances the GM should apply those effects to a character.<br /> <br /> Invoking the Wyrd - Does this take an action or can it be done reflexively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T06:07:01-08:00","id":1166448,"title":"","content":"Delaying your action means precisely that: you opt to take it at any point after your normal initiative for tactical reasons. It's not totally clear because it first refers to holding, and then to yielding, your action. There's also ambiguity in the way it goes on to describe this. It seems to imply you can both act at the end of the turn *and* go first on the next round of combat if you've got a low initiative score. But I don't think that's what it actually means, because otherwise characters who act last naturally would always yield to go first the next round.<br /> <br /> I think holding/yielding is actually aimed at high initiative characters rather than low initiative characters, and is designed to prevent slower characters defending against your attacks. When it says, 'Doing this allows characters with lower initiative scores to act first', what I think it means is: 'Doing this allows a faster character to hold off revealing his action until slower characters have first acted, in order to prevent slower characters defending themselves.'<br /> <br /> The section on shields is definitely unclear. It seems to suggest multiple things: first, that shields can act like armour; then that they can also be a resisted action; then that they're a simple action against firearms. Which is it? <br /> <br /> It seems like a mix of the first and last options. So first you have to make a successful parry roll (only one success required), and if you succeed, then you get to add the shield's full rating as extra armour to your soak roll. Whether extra successes on this parry roll should add to the soak dice too is up to the Storyteller--though I'd probably argue they shouldn't, because you either hold the shield in the way or you don't. It would seem you can only defend against one shooter this way, too, unless you split your dice pool for multiple actions. What you describe is a resisted roll, which this explicitly isn't (but it is how parries normally work in melee).<br /> <br /> The *20 lines have blank lines for custom/rare/niche Abilities at the end of each section on the character sheet (Hobby Talent, Professional Skill, Expert Knowledge). This is where Ride goes--specifically, it would probably fall under 'Professional Skill'. However, you could also rule that it's a Secondary Ability. Rules vary for Secondary Abilities, but they're usually half price OR offer a reduced difficulty (-1, I think) because they're a bit more focused/niche. I always go for the half price thing, since it encourages characters to specialise. As a third option, you could make it a specialty of Animal Ken or Athletics.<br /> <br /> I would argue that for regaining control of a horse, it's Dexterity + Ride, since that's the dicepool it mentions. If it were a different pairing, it would mention it instead of just saying 'a reflexive ride roll'. However, cWoD usually leaves lots of leeway for Attribute + Ability pairings, so you could probably sub in Strength or Wits here if your ST agreed (my rule is that if a player can convince me one pairing should be used over another, I allow it).<br /> <br /> If you're subbing in Animal Ken, then I'd make it Manipulation + Animal Ken or Charisma + Animal Ken, depending on how the rider interacts with her horse (firmness and cajoling versus charm and placating).<br /> <br /> Medicine - This happens a lot. If in doubt, Golden Rule it. Other books do have systems for Medicine, I think, but I could be wrong. I'm pretty sure I read something about first aid and healing somewhere, but I may have imagined it. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd use Wits + Medicine for triage (stops a character bleeding to death if they've lost their last health level) or for temporarily reducing dicepool penalties from injury for a period of time (maybe one success equals either one die restored or one extra turn for the reduced penalty). You could diagnose with Intelligence + Medicine. Heal damage quicker (maybe reduce the healing time of one health level by one step for each success rolled, so that if you roll three successes, the last three health levels each heal one step faster). Understand the effects of a drug. Figure out whether a character has been poisoned. Plenty of uses. It's just sadly left up to the ST.<br /> <br /> The Rhapsody write-up specifically says it's two points of Glamour for each success rolled, but this is shared between all changelings present when the artwork is destroyed. Let's say four changelings put two points in each, so the ST rolls Manipulation + Expression + 8 dice (difficulty 7). That nets, say, 12 successes. Each changeling would only get three points of Glamour. However, if one of the changelings decided to sneak into the artist's studio and destroy the artwork without his friends present, he could take the whole lot (up to his maximum Glamour pool) and the rest would be wasted.<br /> <br /> Yes, Rhapsody really isn't worth it, and it never has been. Mind you, most Musings require lots of time and attention for little reward too, so it's not just Rhapsody that suffers. Only Revelry is really worth it, but that can only be done once per story.<br /> <br /> My personal hack has been to allow characters to roll Glamour + Dreamers once per session, so long as they're maintaining ongoing connections with the humans they've been Musing, to regain one point per success (difficulty 6 if they're regularly working on the Musings, 7 if part-time, 8 if they've been flaky). This allows a steady flow of Glamour from people you're Musing, which makes more sense to me anyway, since art is as much about process and inspiration as it is about the finished product.<br /> <br /> Read p.269: the instances relate to a character's Banality rating. So a human with Banality 10 will completely forget her experiences with the fae as soon as they're over. A human with Banality 1 will have Complete Recall. Banality 5 humans will have a Hazy Memory, etc. The effects kick in as soon as the fae exit the scene or they are no longer in the Wyrd-state. Ignore the durations on the table, though, as those refer only to the length of a changeling's coma after chimerical death.<br /> <br /> Invoking the Wyrd takes an action; it's not reflexive. However, you can Unleash instead and automatically invoke the Wyrd alongside your use of an Art (more cost-effective if you can't risk losing a turn in combat).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-10-2017, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T12:32:25-08:00","id":1166515,"title":"","content":"Also, the rules are a *serious* improvement in quality in terms of being consistent than previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:19:01-08:00","id":1166547,"title":"","content":"adambeyoncelowe I appreciate the response. I'm really not a fan of the ST call answer though. I'm asking because I am the ST, as I am for 90% of my group's RPG campaigns. I was hoping for something a bit more concrete and official.<br /> <br /> The delay thing really needs better wording. So if I understand it correctly it basically lets a character either interrupt a slower character's action or hold to go first next round. That sounds workable. As written in worried that slow characters'players will try to &quot;delay&quot;so that they can hear the faster characters actions before deciding what to do, which defeats the whole point of reverse declaration.<br /> <br /> I think we're in the same page with shields.<br /> <br /> I agree that the text implies maintaining control over a Mount is Dex + Ride for the same reason you state, but I really really hate that interpretation. It adds another use to Dex, which already has far too many combat uses compared to the other physical attributes, and it just doesn't make sense. If a mount is in danger of losing its composure, being particularly deft or agile isn't going to calm it. Charisma makes sense (&quot;Whoa girl...&quot;) as does Strength to force it to heel by pulling the reigns. So I think I'll have to house rule that, which I try to avoid.<br /> <br /> Medicine... well Guess I'll also have to house rule that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Rhapsody - I may have an outdated version of the pdf (should really just check strong to see), but I reread the section 5 times and didn't see where it says you get 2 Glamour per creation success, but that seems reasonable so I'll go with it until I hear otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'll have to reread the sections on banality and Unleashing then check back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","user":"Jimalcoatl","date":". 12-10-2017, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:58:57-08:00","id":1166556,"title":"","content":"&quot;The masterpiece the artist creates contains two points of Glamour oer success.&quot;, very last sentence on page 263 of C20.<br /> <br /> So that means if you invest one point of Glamour into a virtuoso you could in theory get back more Glamour than one person could hold. <br /> <br /> Also, since you don't need to form any sort of relationship with the target you could in theory do this many, many times in short order, for say a dancer or musician or some other artist who produces work quickly. A motley of Rhapsodizers could completely ruin a music festival and get more Glamour than they could hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T16:02:34-08:00","id":1166557,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I would caution against just putting gaining Glamour into the background. If you don't want to have Epiphany be a core part of the game give free dots of Holding or some way to access the Dreaming instead. Making Epiphany just simple and backgrounded does the same disservice to the game as making feeding in Vampire backgrounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:40:18-08:00","id":1166582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1166557#post1166557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I would caution against just putting gaining Glamour into the background. If you don't want to have Epiphany be a core part of the game give free dots of Holding or some way to access the Dreaming instead. Making Epiphany just simple and backgrounded does the same disservice to the game as making feeding in Vampire backgrounded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Epipany is bigger than feeding in VtM. It is always a multistep process to get Glamour outside of the Dreaming. Arguably the quickest easier way is Ravaging, which can back fire and is socially unacceptable. All the other forms of Epiphany require greater investment of time and story, even Rhapsody. Heck, the Dreamers background isn't like the herd background; you don't get a bonus to glamour collection rolls, you just know people who are easier to inspire.<br /> <br /> It is not an easy resource to get a hold of outside of a freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:55:55-08:00","id":1166585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1166582#post1166582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually Epipany is bigger than feeding in VtM. It is always a multistep process to get Glamour outside of the Dreaming. Arguably the quickest easier way is Ravaging, which can back fire and is socially unacceptable. All the other forms of Epiphany require greater investment of time and story, even Rhapsody. Heck, the Dreamers background isn't like the herd background; you don't get a bonus to glamour collection rolls, you just know people who are easier to inspire.<br /> <br /> It is not an easy resource to get a hold of outside of a freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ravaging is roughly equivalent to a quick feeding without consent in Vampire. It's frowned upon, a bit risky, and carries consequences, Banality gain for Ravaging, Humanity loss for the feeding.<br /> <br /> Also, every level of Dreamers gives you a bonus success on the first Musing roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T00:22:01-08:00","id":1166646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1166585#post1166585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, every level of Dreamers gives you a bonus success on the first Musing roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that. And apparently got Ravaging and Rhapsody mixed up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T10:52:46-08:00","id":1167960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimalcoatl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1166547#post1166547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">adambeyoncelowe I appreciate the response. I'm really not a fan of the ST call answer though. I'm asking because I am the ST, as I am for 90% of my group's RPG campaigns. I was hoping for something a bit more concrete and official.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but unfortunately it's a common thing in cWoD games. You won't find the same rigorous systems as in CoD. However, it wouldn't be too difficult to port over what works for you from CoD if you need more crunch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The delay thing really needs better wording. So if I understand it correctly it basically lets a character either interrupt a slower character's action or hold to go first next round. That sounds workable. As written in worried that slow characters'players will try to &amp;quot;delay&amp;quot;so that they can hear the faster characters actions before deciding what to do, which defeats the whole point of reverse declaration. </div> </div> </div>I think you're still misreading it. Forget going first next turn--it's not about that. It's about delaying your action so that your enemies can't respond to them or defend, or so you can interrupt a slower player.<br /> <br /> As for epiphany, I don't care what any purists say: I'm making it easier. Vampires don't have to spend weeks or months just to earn a few Blood Points. It's absurd that it can still take months and you might not even replenish your Glamour track. Forget that. <br /> <br /> So long as players are roleplaying their ongoing relationships with Dreamers, I'm happy to let them roll more often. After all, I want to play a fantasy game with faeries and magic, not The Minutiae of Artistic Practice in Andy Warhol's Loft. But then, I still think Musing doesn't quite sit with the rest of the game. It's like they created this vibrant urban fantasy world around myths and the collective unconscious, then forgot, and made the mechanics all about bumming around with tortured artists instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T12:04:55-08:00","id":1167985,"title":"","content":"Getting enough successes on your Kenning roll to Muse more frequently than a Vampire could feed from a given mortal doesn't seem difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T15:40:34-08:00","id":1168032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1167985#post1167985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting enough successes on your Kenning roll to Muse more frequently than a Vampire could feed from a given mortal doesn't seem difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But you still might only get a handful of successes. A vampire can head to a club and get 10 BP within an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T16:24:46-08:00","id":1168045,"title":"","content":"So can a Ravager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T19:03:38-08:00","id":1168091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1167960#post1167960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're still misreading it. Forget going first next turn--it's not about that. It's about delaying your action so that your enemies can't respond to them or defend, or so you can interrupt a slower player.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to disagree simply because of this <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>C20 p 276</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also yield your action and wait to<br /> see what everyone else does first. Doing this allows characters<br /> with lower initiative scores to act first.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:57:06-08:00","id":1168152,"title":"","content":"That last quote of yours means that if a high initiative character yields his action to wait and see what the lower initiative players do he also allows them, characters with lower initiative, to act first, that is before the high initiative player who yielded.<br /> <br /> So holding back your action means you get to act at a lower initiative than you rolled, like if you just want to see what the rest do before acting, but since you wait untill you see others act you naturally act after them. The main use usually is to delay your action so that you can interrupt a lower initiative character or to react to their action instead of acting first. <br /> <br /> Hope that clears the matter a bit even if I find it rather difficult to put in simple terms.<br /> <br /> Edit: I thought it prudent to underline the fact that yielding your turn or holding your action never affects your next turn. So no it doesnt allw you to act first the next round. Such effects in WoD are reserved for supernatural abilities and powers, no normal action can give you an auto-win on initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Clarity 12-17-2017, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T20:05:39-08:00","id":1168465,"title":"","content":"Blood is pretty much the easiest thing to get for supernaturals, so saying &quot;Vampires can just get this many bps&quot; doesn't really matter. I'd say Quint or Gnosis is a better comparison. Gnosis you get either by access to a special place or hunting the right spirits. Quint special place or complicated magical tricks. Considering how many options a Changeling has and that they can do more than one at the same time(Muse one person while ravaging another or hunting Chimera), I'd say they easily crush Mages or CBs on this front.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T08:34:28-08:00","id":1168529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So holding back your action means you get to act at a lower initiative than you rolled, like if you just want to see what the rest do before acting, but since you wait untill you see others act you naturally act after them. The main use usually is to delay your action so that you can interrupt a lower initiative character or to react to their action instead of acting first.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I interpreted the rules initially, but that one sentence made me reconsider that. Looking back on it it looks like you are correct and that sentence's inclusion was just a poor writing choice that threw me off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T05:42:17-08:00","id":1170151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jimalcoatl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1166277-some-c20-questions?p=1168529#post1168529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I interpreted the rules initially, but that one sentence made me reconsider that. Looking back on it it looks like you are correct and that sentence's inclusion was just a poor writing choice that threw me off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's definite subject/object confusion in that section. I had to read it multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood is pretty much the easiest thing to get for supernaturals, so saying &quot;Vampires can just get this many bps&quot; doesn't really matter. I'd say Quint or Gnosis is a better comparison. Gnosis you get either by access to a special place or hunting the right spirits. Quint special place or complicated magical tricks. Considering how many options a Changeling has and that they can do more than one at the same time(Muse one person while ravaging another or hunting Chimera), I'd say they easily crush Mages or CBs on this front. </div> </div> </div>There are a few points I want to make here, but they overlap somewhat. First, I guess it's because mages get to access Quint in down-time ('I spend eight hours meditating at a node...') and Musing is specifically a thing that takes place in game-time instead, which makes it a big part of every game session. Maybe I just notice the Musing more than I do other ways of regaining magic fuel because of that, but I feel like the style of game play in the material isn't supported by that element of the rules. I feel like the systems for Pathos would make more sense for changelings than Musing, since art and creativity are otherwise very minor parts of the setting as presented in all official material (myth and dreams are more central than making art). It's so central to gameplay mechanics, and yet barely there in the official setting material, that it just feels wrong to me. Even regaining Glamour from stepping into dreams would feel more appropriate than creating art. Perhaps if creating art were presented as just one way to harness or manifest dreams, I'd have less of a problem with it. But why doesn't the act of dreaming generate Glamour at all in a game called Changeling: The Dreaming?<br /> <br /> I suppose freeholds are the best analogue for nodes and caerns ('I sleep in the freehold to regain some Glamour.') but freeholds typically produce less Glamour than nodes do Quintessence. Mage had an optional rule that allowed you to gain 1-5 points of Quint per dot instead of the one point per dot, and I guess it's easy enough to port that over to Changeling. Musing just always feels very inefficient to me, especially when compared to cannibalising chimera, but that's just my opinion. It's always surprised me that hunting chimera wasn't presented as a more popular way to regain Glamour, since it's ripe for story hooks and forces characters to engage with the Dreaming. As it is, it presented as something that happens rarely (maybe I'm misremembering).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-24-2017, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}